IMPORT prelude

§ `Bare EQUALS on two SETs is deliberately ambiguous`

-- The builtin __EQUALS__ (FOR ALL A) and the prelude's SET overload both
-- match SET operands, and the checker has no specificity preference, so
-- this errors rather than silently applying order-sensitive structural
-- equality. The blessed spelling is `set equals`.
--
-- If this test ever starts PASSING, the checker has gained a specificity
-- rule; move this #EVAL into ok/set-operators-overloads.l4 (expected TRUE)
-- and celebrate: bare EQUALS on sets has become extensional
-- (SET-OPERATORS-SPEC §D6's original intent).

#EVAL (setFromList (LIST 2, 1, 1)) EQUALS (setFromList (LIST 1, 2))
